           seen in the implementation/tests ("true", "false", "on", "off", "yes", "no"), and
           returns false for non-matching strings. Therefore changing only character case must not
           change the result for any correct implementation. A patch that merely suppresses the crash
           by skipping intended comparisons could violate this relation on accepted literals. */
        Boolean lhs = callToBoolean(explore);
        if (lhs == null) {
